"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/contextMenu(menuItems:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/contextMenu(menuItems:)","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/contextmenu(menuitems:)","role":"symbol","title":"contextMenu(menuItems:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"contextMenu","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"MenuItems","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"menuItems","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MenuItems","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"k